1
00:00:00,070 --> 00:00:04,170
Department settings change how a whole department sees and handles its work.

2
00:00:04,570 --> 00:00:07,289
They deserve the same review as a dispatch procedure.

3
00:00:07,769 --> 00:00:10,789
Open the department menu, then Department Settings.

4
00:00:11,279 --> 00:00:14,930
We are using the fictional Firehouse fifty-one department, but these

5
00:00:14,930 --> 00:00:18,649
controls are equally relevant to a mobile crisis service, a search

6
00:00:18,649 --> 00:00:23,549
team, a patrol company, a wildland contractor, or a plant response team.

7
00:00:24,059 --> 00:00:26,610
Begin by identifying the problem you want to solve.

8
00:00:27,129 --> 00:00:29,370
Is the roster showing stale availability?

9
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:32,549
Are off-duty members receiving unwanted alerts?

10
00:00:33,009 --> 00:00:35,580
Is a module confusing members who do not use it?

11
00:00:36,080 --> 00:00:40,209
Make one deliberate change, save it, and check its effect before

12
00:00:40,209 --> 00:00:42,240
changing several related controls.

13
00:00:42,439 --> 00:00:45,179
The department name identifies this workspace.

14
00:00:45,600 --> 00:00:49,539
The time zone affects local time displays and scheduled work; our

15
00:00:49,539 --> 00:00:51,500
training department uses Central Time.

16
00:00:51,950 --> 00:00:56,099
Use twenty-four-hour time changes how supported screens display the clock.

17
00:00:56,420 --> 00:00:59,350
It does not create twenty-four-hour staffing coverage.

18
00:00:59,750 --> 00:01:03,729
Account Owner identifies the managing account; review ownership

19
00:01:03,760 --> 00:01:07,309
and administrative access in the personnel and security workflows.

20
00:01:07,789 --> 00:01:11,510
Disable Auto-Available controls the automatic behavior described

21
00:01:11,510 --> 00:01:15,740
on this screen: setting personnel status to Available after an hour.

22
00:01:16,129 --> 00:01:19,170
In this lesson we turn that automatic behavior off.

23
00:01:19,539 --> 00:01:22,819
This avoids treating the passage of time as evidence that a person

24
00:01:22,819 --> 00:01:24,409
has finished a long assignment.

25
00:01:24,789 --> 00:01:29,129
It also makes deliberate member updates and supervisor follow-up more important.

26
00:01:29,559 --> 00:01:32,679
Saving the setting is separate from proving the worker’s behavior

27
00:01:32,679 --> 00:01:37,240
over time; this recording verifies the saved configuration, not a

28
00:01:37,240 --> 00:01:39,140
one-hour background-worker test.

29
00:01:39,309 --> 00:01:43,149
Modern notifications selects supported modern notification behavior,

30
00:01:43,339 --> 00:01:44,999
including modern push sounds.

31
00:01:45,370 --> 00:01:49,380
It does not establish a valid device registration or prove delivery.

32
00:01:49,809 --> 00:01:52,950
Review every channel and consumer your department uses.

33
00:01:53,370 --> 00:01:57,659
Require password resets by email directs administrator-initiated member

34
00:01:57,659 --> 00:02:01,609
resets through single-use recovery links instead of an administrator

35
00:02:01,609 --> 00:02:03,150
selecting a member’s password.

36
00:02:03,609 --> 00:02:08,159
Require Security PIN governs sensitive supported assistant and text actions.

37
00:02:08,460 --> 00:02:11,449
These are security decisions, and the owning administrator

38
00:02:11,449 --> 00:02:14,660
needs to review recovery arrangements and member enrollment.

39
00:02:14,980 --> 00:02:18,320
We leave their existing values visible and discuss their impact

40
00:02:18,320 --> 00:02:19,820
without changing credentials.

41
00:02:20,219 --> 00:02:23,710
T T S Language selects the application’s voice-prompt language.

42
00:02:23,960 --> 00:02:27,131
Under Sorting, we choose LastName for personnel.

43
00:02:27,581 --> 00:02:29,970
Units and calls have their own order settings.

44
00:02:30,331 --> 00:02:33,420
This is useful when a dispatcher knows the member’s surname and

45
00:02:33,420 --> 00:02:34,901
needs a predictable roster.

46
00:02:35,361 --> 00:02:38,620
The Address section describes the department base or office.

47
00:02:39,061 --> 00:02:40,441
Our address is fictional.

48
00:02:40,910 --> 00:02:44,250
Default Map Center accepts decimal latitude and longitude.

49
00:02:44,701 --> 00:02:49,181
Explicit coordinates pin the starting point; leaving both blank lets the system

50
00:02:49,181 --> 00:02:51,230
work out a center from the saved address.

51
00:02:51,701 --> 00:02:55,211
A department center is a map starting point, not a live unit

52
00:02:55,211 --> 00:02:59,151
location, a patrol boundary, or proof that a resource is present.

53
00:02:59,611 --> 00:03:04,491
A search team can use its base, a security company its operational office, and an

54
00:03:04,491 --> 00:03:07,021
industrial team its facility access point.

55
00:03:07,451 --> 00:03:11,190
For a contractor deployment, review whether the department center or an

56
00:03:11,190 --> 00:03:13,210
incident-specific view is appropriate.

57
00:03:13,451 --> 00:03:17,970
Personnel Staffing Reset and Personnel Status Reset are different controls.

58
00:03:18,420 --> 00:03:22,990
Staffing describes availability; status describes current activity.

59
00:03:23,541 --> 00:03:27,310
Our example enables the daily staffing reset at eight a m and

60
00:03:27,310 --> 00:03:29,430
selects Unavailable as its target.

61
00:03:29,930 --> 00:03:33,321
Members then need to declare their availability after the reset.

62
00:03:33,770 --> 00:03:36,971
This can help a volunteer search department avoid relying on

63
00:03:36,971 --> 00:03:41,731
yesterday’s availability, or a wildland contractor require a fresh crew check.

64
00:03:42,090 --> 00:03:45,381
It can also disrupt a team working overnight if the time and

65
00:03:45,381 --> 00:03:47,390
target do not fit its procedures.

66
00:03:47,820 --> 00:03:50,791
The daily status reset remains off in this example.

67
00:03:51,221 --> 00:03:55,561
Consider extended searches, patrol assignments, mental health responses

68
00:03:55,601 --> 00:03:59,971
and plant incidents before automatically replacing a current activity status.

69
00:04:00,410 --> 00:04:04,500
When you create custom personnel staffing or status sets, revisit these

70
00:04:04,500 --> 00:04:08,881
target selections; the intended label must resolve to the current option.

71
00:04:09,051 --> 00:04:12,580
The staffing suppression section lets the department select staffing

72
00:04:12,580 --> 00:04:15,960
levels that should be muted by supported notification paths.

73
00:04:16,340 --> 00:04:19,071
We enable suppression and select Unavailable.

74
00:04:19,590 --> 00:04:23,601
Review the interaction carefully: at the daily reset, members are

75
00:04:23,601 --> 00:04:27,341
marked Unavailable, and supported notifications can suppress them

76
00:04:27,370 --> 00:04:28,971
until their staffing is updated.

77
00:04:29,360 --> 00:04:34,030
This reduces off-duty noise, but a stale staffing declaration can exclude

78
00:04:34,030 --> 00:04:35,760
the person you intended to reach.

79
00:04:36,141 --> 00:04:39,120
For security, the procedure might distinguish on-duty

80
00:04:39,120 --> 00:04:40,960
patrol from off-duty staff.

81
00:04:41,321 --> 00:04:44,611
A mobile response service might distinguish the scheduled response

82
00:04:44,611 --> 00:04:46,190
team from the broader roster.

83
00:04:46,541 --> 00:04:51,041
An industrial team might distinguish the current plant E R T from other employees.

84
00:04:51,481 --> 00:04:54,631
Verify the intended recipients and fallback procedures.

85
00:04:55,091 --> 00:04:59,551
This isolated training stack does not send real alerts, so this lesson does

86
00:04:59,551 --> 00:05:01,710
not claim an external delivery test.

87
00:05:01,921 --> 00:05:04,481
Click Save, then reopen the settings.

88
00:05:04,960 --> 00:05:10,090
In this build the department form does not show a useful success banner, so reopening

89
00:05:10,090 --> 00:05:11,901
is an important persistence check.

90
00:05:12,340 --> 00:05:16,901
Our saved values show Disable Auto-Available checked, LastName sorting,

91
00:05:17,151 --> 00:05:22,391
daily staffing reset enabled at eight a m to Unavailable, daily status reset off,

92
00:05:22,611 --> 00:05:24,721
and suppression enabled for Unavailable.

93
00:05:25,170 --> 00:05:28,121
These are the values actually retained by the application.

94
00:05:28,590 --> 00:05:32,480
Force Department Update requests a department cache refresh if clients

95
00:05:32,480 --> 00:05:34,481
retain stale department information.

96
00:05:34,891 --> 00:05:37,841
Read its timing notice and allow clients to refresh or

97
00:05:37,841 --> 00:05:39,461
sign in again where appropriate.

98
00:05:39,950 --> 00:05:43,321
A cache refresh is not a substitute for saving a form or

99
00:05:43,321 --> 00:05:44,931
testing a notification channel.

100
00:05:45,321 --> 00:05:48,351
Investigate the owning screen and saved value first.

101
00:05:48,561 --> 00:05:50,061
Open Department Modules.

102
00:05:50,461 --> 00:05:54,260
These switches control supported module availability and navigation.

103
00:05:54,661 --> 00:05:58,930
Turning a module on does not purchase its add-on, grant missing permissions,

104
00:05:59,091 --> 00:06:01,100
or configure an external provider.

105
00:06:01,520 --> 00:06:03,631
We turn Calendar off and save.

106
00:06:04,011 --> 00:06:07,150
The page confirms the module settings were saved, and Calendar

107
00:06:07,150 --> 00:06:08,681
disappears from the side menu.

108
00:06:09,281 --> 00:06:12,640
We then turn Calendar back on, save, and reopen it.

109
00:06:13,091 --> 00:06:15,771
The three original training events are still present.

110
00:06:16,070 --> 00:06:18,841
Disabling the module did not delete those records.

111
00:06:19,191 --> 00:06:22,321
The screen also warns that propagation can differ across

112
00:06:22,321 --> 00:06:26,310
features, so review the screens and apps your department actually uses.

113
00:06:26,801 --> 00:06:31,241
For your practice exercise, select one behavior, explain who it affects,

114
00:06:31,461 --> 00:06:35,141
save it in a training department, reopen it and inspect the result.

115
00:06:35,511 --> 00:06:39,700
Document the responsible reviewer and an operational test for any effect

116
00:06:39,700 --> 00:06:41,781
this configuration check cannot prove.
